                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Only bought it because I got a coupon for it. Was only appealing to me for the rare achievements. In both cases still not worth it. \r\nGameplay is... functional... but there was a lot that is unclear about it. The overall experience is a bit frustrating with how repetitive and RNG dependent it is (those explosive guys are totally unfair because there is no way to dodge them when you unlock the cage). Didn't like the fact that the runs were under a time limit for seemingly no reason. Also, the controls feel very sluggish and combat is a pain.\r\n*Might* be considered fun if there was an endless mode to it so there would be a bit more challenge, give the leaderboard a real reason to exist, and make the achievements a little bit less of a grind to complete, but that's a strong maybe on that one. I know that's not likely to happen at this point, though.\r\n\r\nWould say it's only 4/10. Consider passing on this one if you come across it.",
